{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/503424-would-you-buy-a-translated-vienna-by-night","id":503424,"title":"Would you buy a translated Vienna by Night?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-04T14:00:10-07:00","id":503424,"title":"Would you buy a translated Vienna by Night?","content":"What it says on the tin. (And inspired by<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/502624-the-tremere-council-of-seven?p=503082#post503082\"> this post</a>.)<br /> <br /> Would you purchase a translated Feder &amp; Schwert's <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/63467/Wiener-Blut-Wien-bei-Nacht\" target=\"_blank\">Vienna by Night</a>?<br /> <br /> Would crowdfunding work better, or pre-orders?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> I love the picture on page on page 4 of the preview doc.<br /> <br /> You know it's bad if <b>Etrius</b> &amp; <b>Goratrix</b> are working together. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 05-04-2015, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T14:04:34-07:00","id":503465,"title":"","content":"I would for sure. But then, I own just about every By Night book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:57:08-07:00","id":503575,"title":"","content":"Yes, same for me. I must have alll of the By Night series, ALL OF THEM!<br /> <br /> And I think crowdfunding would work fine for it. A translation and print job (with no new artwork or anything) would require a very modest goal, and I am sure that could be reached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5922-volesus","user":"Volesus","date":".  More info 05-04-2015, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5922-volesus","name":"Volesus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T23:20:46-07:00","id":503872,"title":"","content":"I would buy at least the pdf of the translated book. Also Frankfurt by Night, Aachen by Night and that changeling supplement they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T23:35:57-07:00","id":503876,"title":"","content":"Just throwing my voice in agreement as well. I would love to see translated versions of all of the books that weren't printed in English.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T01:00:02-07:00","id":503911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/503424-would-you-buy-a-translated-vienna-by-night?p=503872#post503872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would buy at least the pdf of the translated book. Also Frankfurt by Night, Aachen by Night and that changeling supplement they did.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They don't even seem to offer Frankfurt in the original German in pdf yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/567-patrick","name":"Patrick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar567_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T01:13:04-07:00","id":503915,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a Paris by Night in french or was that a fan supplement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T02:12:21-07:00","id":503999,"title":"","content":"There's a France of Tenebres (France of Darkness), a general supplement about France for Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Wraith and Changeling, published by Ludis editorial. The Paris by Night is another suplement but it wasn't published by Ludis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://kobold.free.fr/kobold/fanz2/img/tenebr.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://kobold.free.fr/kobold/fanz2/img/tenebr.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://kobold.free.fr/kobold/fanz2/img/tenebr.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://kobold.free.fr/kobold/fanz2/img/tenebr.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> These supplements were translated to spanish too, by fans.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T13:16:02-07:00","id":505998,"title":"","content":"Just to echo what I said in response to the post linked above, yes, I would be happy to pay for an English version of Vienna... That said, I can't say how MUCH I'd be willing to pay. :\\","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T13:22:08-07:00","id":506006,"title":"","content":"Good thing I'm german :P<br /> <br /> That said, personally I'm not too interested in Vienna by Night (haven't read it yet), since the setting is bound to be too dominated by the tremere. So it's probably great for an all Tremere chronicle, but otherwise I think it is of somewhat limited use. Are there even non Tremere chars in there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T13:27:05-07:00","id":506014,"title":"","content":"I would definitely buy it! I bought the German pdf, but my German is so rusty I haven't managed to make much sense out of it. I'd love to read the writeup of Valerianus (4th gen Ventrue, childe of Tinia, supposedly dead by 1230 AD according to DAE, but apparently faked his death somehow). I guess I need to hand type the bio into Google Translate some time soon...<br /> <br /> / Ho Dracon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/390-ho-dracon","name":"Ho Dracon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar390_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T13:31:49-07:00","id":506019,"title":"","content":"I splurged $12 on a pdf whose language I can only read half-mangled through online translators, and considered it a worthy purchase. I'd happily spend that much again on a version in fully intelligible English.<br /> <br /> The By Nights are like Pokemon for me. Gotta catch 'em all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T14:35:55-07:00","id":506092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/503424-would-you-buy-a-translated-vienna-by-night#post503424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it says on the tin. (And inspired by<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/502624-the-tremere-council-of-seven?p=503082#post503082\"> this post</a>.)<br /> <br /> Would you purchase a translated Feder &amp; Schwert's <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/63467/Wiener-Blut-Wien-bei-Nacht\" target=\"_blank\">Vienna by Night</a>?<br /> <br /> Would crowdfunding work better, or pre-orders?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you miss the most important question: Will CCP allow you to publish a translated &quot;Wiener Blut&quot;? The answer is most probably &quot;No way in hell!&quot; Even official licensees (like Ulisses Spiele for the German edition of V20) have strict guidelines to follow. Very strict guidelines. Not to mention the licence fee CCP demands. So the very thought of getting the permission to publish a selfmade translation of an old WoD sourcebook is quite honestly next to absurd.<br /> I have translated &quot;Ghouls&quot; into German, a friend of mine did the layout, and at a Games Fair I had the opportunity to talk to a very nice person of Ulisses Spiele. I asked him if there was a way to legally give the final product to German fans, albeit for free. No crowdfunding, no pre-orders, no money involved. I just wanted to give the fans the opportunity to benefit from something I just for fun put a lot of work in. He explicitely discouraged me to even try! I won't repeat what he told me as some of his comments seemed... off the records. But he left no doubt that it borders on insanity to try something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Growing old is mandatory<br /> Growing up is optional</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2578-donovan-rivers","name":"Donovan Rivers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T15:15:07-07:00","id":506125,"title":"","content":"Please allow me to clarify.<br /> <br /> I have zero interest in publishing my own translation.<br /> <br /> I want to give my money to CCP and Feder &amp; Schwert for the translated book.<br /> <br /> I am asking if others would do the same.<br /> <br /> This Post's intent is to generate interest in what would be a profitable and fun business venture for all involved.<br /> <br /> Would you be interested in this theoretical purchase, Donovan Rivers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:16:52-07:00","id":506244,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, i most certainly would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T02:12:35-07:00","id":506579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/503424-would-you-buy-a-translated-vienna-by-night?p=506125#post506125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please allow me to clarify.<br /> <br /> I have zero interest in publishing my own translation.<br /> <br /> I want to give my money to CCP and Feder &amp; Schwert for the translated book.<br /> <br /> I am asking if others would do the same.<br /> <br /> This Post's intent is to generate interest in what would be a profitable and fun business venture for all involved.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then allow me to clarify. CCP will under no circumstances agree to what you have in mind. I'm quite certain of that. The official licencee for the German WoD is Ulisses Spiele, and even they are not allowed to publish anything beside the books covered by their licence. They are not allowed to reprint any of the old German WoD publications, and the same applies to new WoD books (like &quot;Lore of the Clans&quot;). One of the stretch goals of the recent German V20 campaign was a plain and simple pad of character sheets. Not covered by the licence, had to be canceled <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Ulisses offered a Ultra-Deluxe version of the rulebook (genuine leather and God knows what else they had in mind) - not covered by the licence, had to be canceled at the eleventh hour <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. A pdf of the character sheet will be available on the Ulisses homepage, but a fillable pdf will not be available as it isn't (you guessed it) covered by the licence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> It's not just a matter of &quot;I give them money, and they publish the book we want&quot;. It's a matter of what is covered by the licence agreement. &quot;Wiener Blut&quot; definitively isn't covered at all, and to add it to the portfolio would cost lots of money (probably more than we would imagine) and time to negotiate a new agreement.<br /> <br /> So let me ask again: Do you really think there is any chance that CCP will agree to your plan of a translated &quot;Vienna by Night&quot;...?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/503424-would-you-buy-a-translated-vienna-by-night?p=506125#post506125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you be interested in this theoretical purchase, Donovan Rivers?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I wouldn't as I'm German and own the original sourcebook.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Growing old is mandatory<br /> Growing up is optional</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2578-donovan-rivers","name":"Donovan Rivers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T06:07:19-07:00","id":506687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/503424-would-you-buy-a-translated-vienna-by-night#post503424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it says on the tin. (And inspired by<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/502624-the-tremere-council-of-seven?p=503082#post503082\"> this post</a>.)<br /> <br /> Would you purchase a translated Feder &amp; Schwert's <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/63467/Wiener-Blut-Wien-bei-Nacht\" target=\"_blank\">Vienna by Night</a>?<br /> <br /> Would crowdfunding work better, or pre-orders?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> I love the picture on page on page 4 of the preview doc.<br /> <br /> You know it's bad if <b>Etrius</b> &amp; <b>Goratrix</b> are working together. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, yeah<br /> <br /> I almost tried to learn German only for the sake of reading it \u00b0__\u00b0","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin: